<h2 class="section-title">Five Forces Reshaping Opportunity</h2>

<div class="grid">

<div class="card">
<h3>Demographic Reality</h3>
<p>
Many countries face aging populations while others
have expanding workforces. Population structure
changes labor markets, taxation, housing demand,
and future economic growth.
</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Water & Agriculture</h3>
<p>
Food production depends on stable water systems.
Regions that solve water challenges gain long-term
strategic advantages.
</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Infrastructure Power</h3>
<p>
Ports, rail systems, roads, energy grids,
and internet connectivity often determine
economic competitiveness more than politics.
</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Technology Sovereignty</h3>
<p>
Semiconductors, AI systems, automation,
and advanced manufacturing increasingly
shape national influence.
</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Talent Competition</h3>
<p>
Countries compete for entrepreneurs,
engineers, scientists, and skilled workers.
Human capital is becoming the most valuable resource.
</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Supply Chain Control</h3>
<p>
Control of shipping routes, logistics,
energy networks, and critical resources
creates enormous strategic leverage.
</p>
</div>

</div>

<h2 class="section-title">Opportunity Migration Simulator</h2>

<div class="simulation-grid">

<div class="sim-card">
